  "limitations": [
    "Bounded synthetic LiteRoad world (flat ground, clear daylight, painted lanes, orange/white obstacles); results are not evidence about real roads or real vehicles.",
    "Perception source synthetic_rgb_cv is a classical colour/geometry pixel algorithm tuned to LiteRoad renders; it is not YOLOPv2 and inherits no learned-model accuracy claim.",
    "Obstacle distances are flat-ground inverse-perspective estimates from the static synthetic calibration, not metric depth; ttc_seconds is not computed.",
    "Ego localization is simulator telemetry (allowed runtime input); collisions, lateral deviation and route progress in this report are measured by the evaluator after each step and were never used for control.",
    "No traffic rules, junction right-of-way, other moving traffic or pedestrians are modelled.",
    "Simulator-only commands; nothing is sent to a physical vehicle.",
    "Each scenario uses one fixed route; seeds vary the initial pose (+-0.3 m, +-0.04 rad) and obstacle placement (+-3 m along, +-0.3 m across). Wider operating domains are not evaluated.",
    "Wall-clock timings depend on the host CPU and concurrent load; they are measurements, not guarantees."
  ],
